  "label": "child is the one who likes to play outside",
  "description": "The text 'i like to play outside' is overlaid on the image of a child who is visibly happy and outdoors. The child's joyful expression and outdoor setting create an analogical mapping where the child (visual entity) is understood to be the 'i' (textual entity) in the statement. The mapping is direct: the child represents the subject of the text, embodying the sentiment expressed. This is a classic case of visual material being mapped onto textual material to convey identity or role.",
